title: pidly claim / release, and the lock
desc:21
claim writes the agent's pid into line 1; release blanks it back to "claim:".
Both rewrite info, as does edit, so all three serialize behind a lock.

The lock is a file created with O_EXCL, carrying the holder's pid. Creation
and ownership must be one operation: an earlier design used a lock directory
with the pid in a file inside it, and the gap between the two let 4 of 30
racing claims win. An empty lock means a holder mid-write, never an abandoned
one, and must not be broken.

The pid recorded in a claim is the agent's, from PIDLY_PID, not the pidly
process's — pidly claim exits immediately, so its own pid would read as stale
at once. Release requires ownership; a dead local claim is reap's job.

claim also refuses a ticket whose needs are not all closed.

Done: implemented in bin/pidly, covered by tests/claim.sh (17 cases including
a 30-way race).
